[2026/05/15 22:52:26] [DEBUG] isgsa.backend/openai: [cyan]Raw func call response: Choice(finish_reason='tool_calls', index=0, logprobs=None, message=ChatCompletionMessage(content=None, refusal=None, role='assistant', annotations=[], audio=None, function_call=None, tool_calls=[ChatCompletionMessageFunctionToolCall(id='call_0YupjGbM0olIcDDuf7fk5dil', function=Function(arguments='{"nl_text":"I will build a compact LensKit 0.14.4 experiment pipeline that loads the three provided implicit-feedback datasets, applies 5-core filtering, and converts MovieLens and Amazon ratings >3 into binary interactions. For each dataset I will generate five fixed random seeds and perform a user-based 80/20 holdout by sampling 20% of each user’s interactions into test whenever possible, ensuring train users remain aligned with the evaluation protocol. I will train three simple baselines with standard settings—ALS, ItemKNN, and Pop—using LensKit implementations and recommend top-N items from the train-candidate pool excluding seen items. The evaluation will compute Precision@k and nDCG@k for k in {1,5,10} on each dataset/algorithm/seed combination, then aggregate results into per-condition means and standard deviations. For a short statistical analysis, I will run a one-way repeated comparison across seeds by summarizing metric variability and also report paired seed-level differences between algorithms within each dataset as a lightweight significance check. To satisfy reproducibility and reporting needs, all raw results and summary tables will be saved to the working directory as NumPy and CSV artifacts. I will also generate concise visualizations showing metric distributions across random seeds for each dataset and algorithm, which directly quantify split-seed sensitivity. The script will execute end-to-end at global scope, print the evaluation outputs and variability summaries, and save the experiment_data structure as required.","code":"import os\\nworking_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'working\')\\nos.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)\\n\\nimport warnings\\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\'ignore\')\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport pandas as pd\\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\nfrom scipy import stats\\n\\nfrom lenskit.algorithms import Recommender\\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.basic import Popular\\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.als import ImplicitMF\\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.item_knn import ItemItem\\n\\nexperiment_data = {\\n    \'ml100k\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': []},\\n    \'amazon_vg\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': []},\\n    \'lastfm\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': []},\\n}\\n\\nseeds = [1, 7, 21, 42, 84]\\nTOPK = [1, 5, 10]\\nREC_K = max(TOPK)\\n\\ndef ensure_cols(df):\\n    cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\\n    if \'user\' not in cols or \'item\' not in cols:\\n        raise ValueError(f\'Expected user/item columns, got {df.columns.tolist()}\')\\n    out = df.rename(columns={cols[\'user\']: \'user\', cols[\'item\']: \'item\'})[[\'user\', \'item\']].copy()\\n    return out\\n\\ndef k_core_filter(df, min_u=5, min_i=5):\\n    df = df[[\'user\', \'item\']].drop_duplicates().copy()\\n    while True:\\n        uc = df.groupby(\'user\').size()\\n        ic = df.groupby(\'item\').size()\\n        good_u = uc[uc >= min_u].index\\n        good_i = ic[ic >= min_i].index\\n        ndf = df[df[\'user\'].isin(good_u) & df[\'item\'].isin(good_i)]\\n        if len(ndf) == len(df):\\n            break\\n        df = ndf\\n    return df.reset_index(drop=True)\\n\\ndef load_ml100k(path=\'u.data\'):\\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, sep=\'\\\\t\', header=None, names=[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\'])\\n    df = df[df[\'rating\'] > 3][[\'user\', \'item\']].drop_duplicates()\\n    return k_core_filter(df)\\n\\ndef load_amazon(path=\'VideoGames.csv\'):\\n    try:\\n        df = pd.read_csv(path)\\n        cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\\n        ucol = next((cols[c] for c in cols if c in [\'user\', \'userid\', \'reviewerid\']), None)\\n        icol = next((cols[c] for c in cols if c in [\'item\', \'asin\', \'productid\']), None)\\n        rcol = next((cols[c] for c in cols if c in [\'rating\', \'overall\', \'score\']), None)\\n        if ucol is None or icol is None or rcol is None:\\n            raise ValueError(\'CSV columns not detected; falling back to headerless parse\')\\n        df = df.rename(columns={ucol: \'user\', icol: \'item\', rcol: \'rating\'})\\n    except Exception:\\n        df = pd.read_csv(path, header=None)\\n        if df.shape[1] < 3:\\n            raise ValueError(\'VideoGames.csv must contain at least user,item,rating columns\')\\n        df = df.iloc[:, :3]\\n        df.columns = [\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\']\\n    df = df[df[\'rating\'] > 3][[\'user\', \'item\']].drop_duplicates()\\n    return k_core_filter(df)\\n\\ndef load_lastfm(path=\'user_taggedartists-timestamps.dat\'):\\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, sep=\'\\\\t\')\\n    cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\\n    ucol = next((cols[c] for c in cols if \'user\' in c), None)\\n    icol = next((cols[c] for c in cols if \'artist\' in c or c == \'item\'), None)\\n    if ucol is None or icol is None:\\n        raise ValueError(f\'Could not detect LastFM columns in {df.columns.tolist()}\')\\n    df = df.rename(columns={ucol: \'user\', icol: \'item\'})[[\'user\', \'item\']].drop_duplicates()\\n    return k_core_filter(df)\\n\\ndef user_holdout(df, test_frac=0.2, seed=42):\\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\\n    test_parts = []\\n    train_parts = []\\n    for _, g in df.groupby(\'user\', sort=False):\\n        n = len(g)\\n        n_test = max(1, int(round(n * test_frac))) if n >= 2 else 0\\n        n_test = min(n_test, n - 1) if n >= 2 else 0\\n        idx = np.arange(n)\\n        if n_test > 0:\\n            test_idx = set(rng.choice(idx, size=n_test, replace=False).tolist())\\n            mask = np.array([i in test_idx for i in idx])\\n            test_parts.append(g.iloc[mask])\\n            train_parts.append(g.iloc[~mask])\\n        else:\\n            train_parts.append(g)\\n    train = pd.concat(train_parts, ignore_index=True)\\n    test = pd.concat(test_parts, ignore_index=True) if test_parts else pd.DataFrame(columns=df.columns)\\n    return train, test\\n\\ndef precision_at_k(recs, truth, k):\\n    rec_k = recs[:k]\\n    if k == 0:\\n        return 0.0\\n    return sum(1 for x in rec_k if x in truth) / float(k)\\n\\ndef ndcg_at_k(recs, truth, k):\\n    rec_k = recs[:k]\\n    dcg = 0.0\\n    for i, it in enumerate(rec_k):\\n        if it in truth:\\n            dcg += 1.0 / np.log2(i + 2)\\n    ideal_hits = min(len(truth), k)\\n    if ideal_hits == 0:\\n        return 0.0\\n    idcg = sum(1.0 / np.log2(i + 2) for i in range(ideal_hits))\\n    return dcg / idcg\\n\\ndef evaluate_algo(algo, train, test, name):\\n    rec_algo = Recommender.adapt(algo)\\n    rec_algo.fit(train)\\n    train_items = set(train[\'item\'].unique())\\n    truth = test.groupby(\'user\')[\'item\'].apply(set).to_dict()\\n    users = list(truth.keys())\\n    rows = []\\n    preds_store = []\\n    gt_store = []\\n    for u in users:\\n        try:\\n            recs = rec_algo.recommend(u, REC_K)\\n            rec_items = [] if recs is None or len(recs) == 0 else [x for x in recs[\'item\'].tolist() if x in train_items]\\n        except Exception:\\n            rec_items = []\\n        gt = truth[u]\\n        preds_store.append((u, rec_items))\\n        gt_store.append((u, list(gt)))\\n        row = {\'user\': u}\\n        for k in TOPK:\\n            row[f\'precision@{k}\'] = precision_at_k(rec_items, gt, k)\\n            row[f\'ndcg@{k}\'] = ndcg_at_k(rec_items, gt, k)\\n        rows.append(row)\\n    res = 